      "title": "Norway’s King Harald dies leaving stormy succession over crown princess’s Epstein links",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/28/norway-king-harald-dies-leaving-stormy-succession-mette-marit-crown-princesss-epstein-links",
      "description": "<p>Crown Prince Haakon’s wife, Mette-Marit, corresponded with late US sex offender between 2011 and 2014, long after he was convicted</p><p>King Harald V of Norway has died at the age of 89, the palace in Oslo has announced, triggering the succession of his son, Haakon, whose wife Mette-Marit’s association with Jeffrey Epstein has sparked fierce recent controversy.</p><p>“It is with deep sadness that we announce that His Majesty King Harald passed away today. King Harald passed away peacefully at Oslo University Hospital on Friday, August 28 at 6.35 am,” the palace said in a statement.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/28/norway-king-harald-dies-leaving-stormy-succession-mette-marit-crown-princesss-epstein-links\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-28T07:18:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "Harald V, Norway’s King as Tradition and Modernity Collided, Dies at 89",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/28/world/europe/king-harald-v-dead.html",
      "description": "His 35-year reign opened an ancient monarchy to marriages with so-called commoners and to an incendiary association with Jeffrey Epstein.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-08-28T07:01:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "King Harald V, Norway's longest-serving monarch, passes away at 89",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/king-harald-v-norway-s-longest-serving-monarch-passes-away-at-89-126082800487_1.html",
      "description": "King Harald V of Norway, who went into exile in the United States as a child during the Nazi occupation of his homeland and refused a string of European noblewomen in order to marry his school sweetheart, has died. He was 89.\nThe palace announced his death Friday morning.\nHarald was Europe's oldest monarch. The popular king modernised the royal house but refused to follow in the footsteps of other aging monarchs who have abdicated in recent times. His son now automatically becomes King Haakon VIII.\nLike other royal houses in Europe, the Norwegian monarchs serve a largely symbolic role, enjoying celebrity status while real power in the democracy of 5.5 million rests with an elected parliament. Harald was crowned king after his British-born father, King Olav V, died in January 1991, and reigned during an oil-and-gas-driven economic boom in his country.\nHarald was born in 1937 in Asker, near Oslo, becoming the first Norwegian prince to be born in the country since King Olav IV in 1370",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-28T07:20:00"
    },
